Package: laridae
Type: Package
Title: Constrained Triangulation and Meshing with CGAL
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Michael D.", "Sumner", , "mdsumner@gmail.com", c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Mark", "Padgham", role = "ctb"), person("The CGAL Project", role = "cph") )
Description: A persistent constrained Delaunay triangulation handle backed by
    the 'CGAL' (Computational Geometry Algorithms Library) classes
    'Constrained_triangulation_plus_2' and 'Delaunay_mesher_2' (The CGAL
    Project (2026) <https://doc.cgal.org/6.2.1/Manual/packages.html>).
    Points and constraint segments can be inserted and removed at any time,
    crossing constraints are resolved by inserting the crossing, and the
    mesh can be refined by minimum angle, maximum area, or a sizing field
    that varies with position. Input and output follow the vertices /
    segments / triangles contract shared with 'cdtr', including
    per-triangle constraint depth.
